{title: Suraj Ki Garmi Se}
{artist: Anup Jalota}
{key: C#m}

{c: Verse 1}
[C#m],        jaise suraj ki garmi se jalte hue tan ko
[C#m],        mil jaye taruvar ki chhaya
[F#m],        aisa hi sukh mere man ko mila hai
[F#m] [B],        mai jabse sharan teri aya,
[C#m],        mere ram
[F#m],        bhataka hua mera man tha koi
[B] [C#m],        mil na raha tha sahara
[F#m],        laharo se ladati hui nav ko jaise
[C#m],        mil na raha ho kinara
[A] [C#m],        mil na raha ho kinara
[C#m],        us ladakhdati hui nav ko jo
[C#m],        kisi ne kinara dikhaya
[F#m],        aisa hi sukh mere man ko mila hai
[F#m] [B],        mai jabse sharan teri aya,
[C#m],        mere ram
[F#m],        shital bane aag chandan ke jaisi
[B] [C#m],        raghav kripa ho jo teri
[F#m],        ujiyali punam ki ho jae rate
[C#m],        jo thi amavas andheri,
[A] [C#m],        jo thi amavas andheri
[C#m],        yug-yug se pyasi marubhumi ne
[C#m],        jaise savan ka sades paya
[F#m],        aisa hi sukh mere man ko mila hai
[F#m] [B],        mai jabse sharan teri aya,
[C#m],        mere ram
[F#m],        jis rah ki mazil tera milan ho
[B] [C#m],        us par kadam mai badhau
[F#m],        phulo me kharo me, patjhad baharo me
[A] [C#m],        mai na kabhi dagmagau,
[C#m],        mai na kabhi dagmagau
[C#m],        pani ke pyase ko taqadir ne
[C#m],        jaise ji bhar ke amrit pilaya
[F#m],        aisa hi sukh mere man ko mila hai
[F#m] [B],        mai jabse sharan teri aya,
[C#m],        mere ram
